Task Guide:

Task make_1_lvl1:
Propose a retrosynthesis route to synthesize the molecule with SMILES [CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]. The route must have at least 1 reactions.  You should use the template/s ['1914384'] in this order.

Required submission format:
Submit a JSON object representing the retrosynthesis route. It must follow the same JSON format as the next example: `{
  "type": "mol",
  "smiles": "CO",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "reaction",
      "template_id": 1234,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "BrC"
        },
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "[OH-]"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}`.



You must think what to do next. You can use some of the tools available in the system.

When you think that the task is completed, you can submit the answer.
For that, answer with: "Final Answer: <your answer>". It is very important to follow this format.

The route is valid in format. The reaction is an intramolecular carbonyl-ene cyclization, which converts the keto-alkene precursor into the target trifluoromethyl cyclopentanol with an exocyclic alkene. The schema validation passed.

The precursor `CC(c1ccccc1)=CCCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F` represents the open-chain keto-olefin that undergoes the intramolecular ene reaction to form the target. This matches template 1914384 (intramolecular carbonyl-ene reaction forming the CF3-substituted cyclopentanol).

Final Answer: 
```json
{
  "type": "mol",
  "smiles": "[CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "reaction",
      "template_id": 1914384,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "mol",
          "smiles": "CC(c1ccccc1)=CCCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This route uses template 1914384, an intramolecular carbonyl-ene reaction. The open-chain keto-olefin precursor (1,1,1-trifluoro-7-phenyloct-6-en-2-one) cyclizes to form the target 2-(1-phenylvinyl)-1-(trifluoromethyl)cyclopentan-1-ol, establishing the cyclopentane ring, the tertiary alcohol bearing the CF3 group, and the exocyclic alkene with defined stereochemistry.
